{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-27019",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255329/assets/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The zeros of the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ occur at $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n.$\n\n- Statement II is false. $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$ is a zero of the function.\n\n- Statement III is true. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
